e against a grid lower bound with a 0.7794 A cell slack, chain pair against whole body, no admission rule against the full one), so NOTHING here shows the sampler would admit or reject any deposited complex; comparing 6-7 against 12 is hypothetical arithmetic between two differently defined quantities and calibrates or bounds NOTHING; the acceptance fractions are not orientation-space volume, equilibrium probability or linker feasibility, and the joint covariance for the ratio is missing because the arms share proposals and no joint counts are retained; the four-body design identifies NO controlling variable and neither establishes nor refutes a body-size effect; the census entry list is selected and a zero-contact-band filter is applied BEFORE induced-pair selection, which dropped two ligand-spanned 9MZA pairs (A/B and C/D), so 6 of 15 is not a population rate; the two reported 9MZA interfaces are two related instances inside ONE deposited A2B2 assembly, not two independent systems; the two retained literature indexes have no query, page or total-hit closure and cannot establish an absence in the field; and no selectivity requirement is estimated. ⚠ SUPERSEDED 2026-09-08, RETAINED: the previous claim asserted that a real transcriptional CIP fails this sampler's floor, that the result bounds that floor from above, that the ratio measures orientation-space volume and is monotone in the floor, that body size is not the controlling variable, that the literature sweeps establish a field-wide absence, and that this modality's selectivity requirement is not smaller than a degrader's. All of those are WITHDRAWN. ⚠ SUPERSEDED, RETAINED: the pre-2026-08-07 claim was framed as 'Transcriptional chemically-induced proximity on EWSR1::NR4A3', which implied a disease-specific deliverable it does not carry.",
